      <activity id="8122e945-9137-5530-822d-719daf1a94d9" activityNameId="0ecfb3ac-b15b-5edb-9952-c390c942c9cd" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, railway track</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, railway track
 All data is referred to meter*year. Life time of the rail track infrastructure is assumed to be 100 yrs. Inventory for a conventional gravel track bedding.Data is refers to a two way track.;
UUID: 2f8cf21b-3cfd-4836-9ab7-f68a607bb1ac
The inventory includes the disposal of contaminated gravel (20% of the total amount). About 80% of the gravel is re-used in other activities and thus a cut off allocation has been applied. Transport to disposal and re-use  is accounted for with 200km. For diposal of sleepers a cut off allocation is made. Transport to disposal  is accounted for with 200km.
Location: Data refers to average conditions in Switzerland and a specific conditions in Germany
Technology: Data represents current technologies
Time period: Rail length is based on current statistical data (2000). The expenditures for the track disposal represent a recent high speed track in Germany
Production volume: na
Sampling: national statistics and literature studies 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2f8cf21b-3cfd-4836-9ab7-f68a607bb1ac.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
